# Prices, why they fell, caravans, and more everyday work (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7; the work theme): broad
# scenes nearly any two can have when the topic comes up. topic.what is "a meal" or "herbs" for prices (so "the price
# of #topic.what#" reads right, but never "cheap #topic.what#"), the good itself for a fall's cause ("timber",
# "meals"); topic.who is a name or a look; topic.where is the other town of a caravan. Where an answer changes what
# the last word must be, it sets a mark (#x) and the last word has its own line (a@x).

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Prices up

scene w7c_up_purse
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : I took #topic.price# to market and came home with no change at all. | Have you priced #topic.what# lately? Don't. | My purse is lighter and my basket's lighter. How's that work?
b[wealth=rich] #rich : Is it so much? I suppose it is, for some. | I'll take your word for it. | Magic, I expect.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : I didn't take anything. I hadn't anything to take. | I don't price. I look and walk on. | Mine's been light all year.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Don't look at me. I only pass it on. | Somebody upstream's greedy. Not me. | Costs, #address#. Everyone's costs.
b : Same here. | I have. I wept. | It's a riddle.
a@rich : For most of us. | Do. | Some magic.
a@poor : That's not right. Not right at all. | Wise. | Mine too, now.
a@merch : Someone's passing it on to me. | Somebody always is. | Costs. Aye.
a : It's not right. | Wept, and paid. | A cruel one.

scene w7c_up_blame
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : Whose fault is it, then? #topic.price# for #topic.what#. | Somebody's getting rich off this, and it isn't me. | They say it's the roads. They always say it's the roads.
b[temper=short] : The Houses. It's always the Houses. | Find them and I'll tell them. | Then fix the roads!
b[honesty=sly] : Me. I've been buying it all up. Ha. | Not me. Well. A little me. | It's the roads. Mostly.
b[stage=old] : It was the weather in my day. Now it's the roads. | Nobody's fault. Everybody's fault. | They said it then, too.
b : The carters, I heard. | Someone, somewhere. | And they're right, sometimes.
a : Carters, Houses, the moon. | Somewhere far from here. | Roads, roads.

scene w7c_up_cut_back
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : We'll be cutting back this week. | No more of that till it drops. | I'll have to choose: #topic.what#, or boots.
b[parent=yes] : The pups don't understand cutting back. | We've cut back so far there's no back left. | Mine need both.
b[warmth=warm] #warm : Come and eat with us one night. | I'll share mine. No, I insist. | Boots. Then come to me for #topic.what#.
b : Wise. | Good luck to you. | Boots last longer.
a@warm : You're kind. | If you insist. | I might, at that.
a : Needs must. | Don't I know it. | Boots, then.

scene w7c_up_story
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : I asked for #topic.what# and the stallholder laughed when I counted out my coin. | A wolf ahead of me at the stall just turned round and left. | I heard someone haggle for #topic.what# for half an hour.
b[humour=merry] : Laughed? Laugh back louder. | Wise wolf. I'll follow them. | Did they win?
b[warmth=warm] : That's cruel. I'd not stand for it. | Poor soul. | Good for them. Somebody has to.
b : The cheek of it. | Can't blame them. | And?
a : I laughed too. Then I left. | I nearly did the same. | They saved a penny. Lost the morning.

scene w7c_up_market_talk
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.place=market
a : #topic.price#. Look at the board. #topic.price#! | Every stall's put it up the same. Funny, that. | Shall we buy now, or wait for worse?
b[role=merchant] #merch : Don't shout it. You'll scare the buyers. | Not mine. Mine's honest. Slightly. | Buy now. Tomorrow's dearer.
b : I see it. I wish I didn't. | Not so funny. | Wait. It can't get worse.
a@merch : I'll shout it all I like. | Slightly. | Dearer still? Now, then.
a : I'll see it in my dreams. | Somebody's talking to somebody. | It can. It always can.

scene w7c_up_tavern
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.place=tavern
a : At #topic.price#, I'll be drinking slower. | Cheers to dear prices. | Everything's going up but my #wages#.
b[humour=dry] #dry : Slower drinking. Longer evenings. Every cloud. | Cheers. To our empty purses. | Your #wages# and the river in summer.
b : Drink up while you can. | Cheers. | Ain't that the way.
a@dry : There's that. | Empty, and getting emptier. | Low and lower.
a : I intend to. | #toast#. | Every week.

scene w7c_up_meal
when topic=prices topic.item=meal topic.dir=up
a : #topic.price# for a bowl of stew. A bowl! | The pie-wife wants #topic.price# a pie now. | Last week a meal was cheaper. I counted.
b[job=cook|innkeeper] #cook : And the onions cost me double. Someone has to pay. | Flour's dear. Pies are flour. | Not my doing. I'm losing on it.
b[stage=young] #pup : Can we still have pie? | Is pie a lot of money? | Can I have half a pie?
b : Cook at home, then. | Bake your own. | You counted?
a@cook : Then it's the onions I'll curse. | Pies are pennies, now. | Somebody's not losing.
a@pup : Not this week, little one. | A lot, yes. | We'll see.
a : On what fire? | With what flour? | Every penny.

scene w7c_up_herbs
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=up
a : Herbs at #topic.price#. A cough's a luxury now. | I'll not be ill this month. Can't afford it. | They want #topic.price# for a twist of willow bark.
b[job=healer] #heal : I know. I'm paying it too. Come to me if it's bad. | Don't wait till it's bad. Bad's dearer. | Bark grows by the river, free. Take a knife.
b[stage=old] #old : My knees cost #topic.price# a week now. | Neither will I. I'll lie about it. | I remember it growing on every bank.
b : Gather your own. | Wise. | It's robbery.
a@heal : Bless you. I might. | I'll try not to wait. | Which river? Which bark?
a@old : Mine too, near enough. | Lie well, then. | So do I. Now look.
a : I don't know which is which. | Being ill's for the rich now. | And nobody stops them.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Prices down

scene w7c_down_glad
when topic=prices topic.dir=down
a : #topic.what.capitalize#, #topic.price#! Down! | Something got cheaper. Write down the day. | Good news for the purse. Prices are down.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Gods be thanked. I can eat. | Down? I'll believe it. | My purse needs it.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Lovely. For the buyers. | I'm writing it. With tears. | Not for the seller's.
b[stage=old] : Won't last. Buy now. | I'll remember it. Won't be many. | Down till Restday, maybe.
b : About time. | Marvellous. | Good.
a@merch : Sorry. Not very. | Ha. Sorry. | No. Not for you.
a : Hurry, then. | It's a rare day. | Very good.

scene w7c_down_why
when topic=prices topic.dir=down
a : Why's #topic.what# cheaper? What's wrong with it? | Down to #topic.price#. Somebody's flooding the market. | Cheap. I don't trust cheap.
b[honesty=guarded] #worm : There's a worm in it somewhere. Look. | Somebody's dumping. Wait and see who. | Nor me.
b[humour=merry] : Maybe someone was nice. It happens! Rarely. | Floods are lovely if you've a bucket. | Trust it long enough to buy some.
b : A good harvest, I heard. | Carts came in, I think. | Cheap's cheap.
a@worm : I'll look. | I'll watch. | See? Nobody does.
a : I hope you're right. | Maybe. | Hm. I'll buy a little.

scene w7c_down_stock
when topic=prices topic.dir=down topic.item=herbs a.stage=adult|old
a : I'll stock up while it's #topic.price#. | Buy now and keep it, that's what #mum# did. | At this price, I'll have the cellar full.
b[drive=ambitious] #amb : Buy it all. Sell it back at the turn. | Clever, your mother. | Fill two.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : With what? | Mine did too, when we had a cellar. | What cellar?
b : Good thinking. | Wise woman. | Don't let it spoil.
a@amb : I'm not a merchant. | She was. | Two! Where?
a@poor : Sorry. I didn't think. | Things will turn. | I'll share some with you.
a : I'll try. | She was. | I won't.

scene w7c_down_meal
when topic=prices topic.item=meal topic.dir=down
a : A hot meal for #topic.price#. I'll eat out tonight! | Pie's cheaper. Pie's cheaper! | Supper's on me. At these prices.
b[job=cook|innkeeper] #cook : And who's paying the cook? | Cheaper pies, thinner cook. | Come to mine. I'm matching it.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : I'll have two. | Pie! | I'll hold you to it.
b : Treat yourself. | Pie. Lovely. | Generous.
a@cook : The diners, for once. | You'll survive. | Then I'll come to yours.
a : I will. | Pie for everyone! | It's cheap. I can afford to be.

scene w7c_down_herbs
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=down
a : Herbs are down. My chest'll thank me. | Cheap herbs! I'll buy for the whole winter. | Willow bark at #topic.price#. Glory be.
b[job=healer] #heal : Good. Come and get the right ones. Not the wrong ones. | Dry them well, or they'll rot. | Now folk might come before it's too late.
b : Good. | Clever. | At last.
a@heal : I will. | Well, I'll try. | That's the hope.
a : Isn't it. | Clever? Thrifty. | My chest agrees.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Why it fell

scene w7c_cause_grateful
when topic=price_cause
a : We've #topic.who# to thank for cheaper #topic.what#. | #topic.who# brought #topic.what# in, and down it came. | You know why it's all so cheap? #topic.who#.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Thank them? They've cut my margin to the bone. | And down came my profits. | I know. I'm not pleased.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Bless them. Truly. | And I could buy some. First time this month. | Then bless #topic.who#.
b[honesty=guarded] #doubt : Where'd they get it, though? | Brought it from where? | Hm. I'd ask questions.
b : Well! Good of them. | Lucky us. | Is that so.
a@merch : Somebody's margin had to go. | Your profits, my supper. | You'll live.
a@doubt : I didn't ask. | Who cares where? | Ask away. I'm buying.
a : It was. | Very lucky. | It is.

scene w7c_cause_who
when topic=price_cause topic.known=no
a : A stranger, #topic.who#, came with #topic.what#. | Some traveller sold the shops #topic.what#. #topic.who#, it was. | Did you see #topic.who#? Brought a load of #topic.what#.
b[stage=young] : Are they still here? Can I see? | Was it a pirate? | I saw them! I think.
b[temper=nervy] : Strangers. I don't like strangers. | What else did they bring? | I'll keep my door locked.
b : Never seen them. | Who's that, then? | I missed them.
a : Passing through, I think. | Nobody knows. | Everyone's talking of them.

scene w7c_cause_named
when topic=price_cause topic.known=yes
a : #topic.who# did the town a good turn. #topic.what.capitalize#, cheap. | That #topic.who#'s been bringing #topic.what# in. | Prices fell, and it's #topic.who# did it.
b[pair.band=friends|family] : I always liked them. | Good. They need the trade. | Did they? Good for them.
b : Good of them. | Have they, now? | So I heard.
a : Good sort. | Loads of it. | It's all over town.

scene w7c_cause_more
when topic=price_cause
a : Let's hope they bring more #topic.what#. | I'd pay #topic.who# to come again. | If #topic.who# comes back, prices'll fall again.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Let's hope they don't. | I'd pay them to stay away. | Then I'll shut my stall.
b : I'll drink to that. | Me too. | Here's hoping.
a@merch : You would say that. | I'd pay more. | Sell something else, then.
a : So will I. | We'll pass a hat. | Hoping.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Caravans arrived

scene w7c_cv_in_noise
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : The #topic.where# wagons rolled in. Woke the whole street. | Mules braying since dawn. #topic.where# carts. | You hear them? #topic.where# caravan's in.
b[tired=yes] #tired : I heard. Every wheel. | Mules. I hate mules. | Heard them? I dreamed them.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Lovely sound. Lovely, lovely sound. | Bless those mules. | Music.
b : Worth the noise. | Mules always bray. | I did.
a@tired : Every one. | They hate you too. | Nightmares, then.
a@merch : To you, maybe. | Bless them? Curse them. | Music. Ha.
a : Maybe. | Always. | Who didn't?

scene w7c_cv_in_goods
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : What've they brought from #topic.where#, do you know? | There's cloth on the #topic.where# carts. Good cloth. | Salt fish from #topic.where#, I hope.
b[role=merchant] #merch : My order, gods willing. | I'll have it on my stall by noon. | Hope away. I've bought it all.
b[stage=young] #pup : Sweets? Are there sweets? | Can I have a ribbon? | Fish. Yuck.
b : Everything and nothing. | Good. | Fish!
a@merch : Gods willing. | Save me some. | All of it?
a@pup : Maybe. Ask nicely. | We'll see. | Fish is good for you.
a : Everything, then. | Very. | Fried, with bread. Lovely.

scene w7c_cv_in_news
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : The drivers say the road from #topic.where# was quiet. | Carters from #topic.where# have news. | The #topic.where# lot say prices are worse there.
b[temper=nervy] : Quiet? Truly? | Good news, I hope. | Worse? How?
b : Good. | What news? | Can't be.
a : Truly. | Weddings and weather. | Dearer bread, dearer everything.

scene w7c_cv_in_carters
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : Those carters'll drink the inn dry tonight. | Look at them. Dust from ears to tail. | Poor beasts. They look half dead.
b[job=innkeeper] : Let them. They pay. | I'll have the water hot. | So do the drivers.
b[job=carter] : We earn it. | You'd be dusty too. | That road does it.
b : Let them. | Long road. | Rest them.
a : They will. | Look at the state of them. | Hope they get a night's rest.

## Caravans left

scene w7c_cv_out_wave
when topic=caravan topic.kind=left
a : The #topic.where# wagons pulled out at dawn. | Saw the #topic.where# carts off. Long way. | That's the caravan gone for #topic.where#.
b[warmth=warm] : I hope they make it safe. | Long way for anyone. | Bright One go with them.
b[role=merchant] : My goods on it, too. | I'll not sleep till they're back. | With my coin.
b : Safe road to them. | Long way. | Good.
a : Back by the month's end, they say. | And a hard one, past the hills. | Quieter round here, anyway.

scene w7c_cv_out_quiet
when topic=caravan topic.kind=left
a : Town's quiet with the caravan gone. | No carters in the inn tonight. | Streets are empty without the wagons.
b[job=innkeeper] #inn : Quiet and poor. | No carters, no coin. | Empty, and my till too.
b : Nice, for a change. | Quieter. | I like it.
a@inn : They'll be back. | Not for long. | It'll fill again.
a : You can hear the birds. | Much. | So do I.

## Caravans raided

scene w7c_cv_raid_who
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a : Raided on the #topic.where# road. Do they know who? | Who'd rob a caravan from #topic.where#? Desperate wolves. | The #topic.where# caravan's lost. Bandits.
b[role=guard] #guard : We've an idea. Not enough of us to act on it. | Desperate, and armed. | Lost, and we were told too late.
b[stage=old] : There's always someone. | Hungry ones. | It's always the same.
b : Nobody knows. | Bandits. | Terrible.
a@guard : Then get more. | And bold, to go for a caravan. | Too late. Always.
a : Somebody must. | Hungry, or wicked. | Those poor drivers.

scene w7c_cv_raid_prices
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a : Prices will jump now. Mark me. | No goods from #topic.where# for a month, I'd bet. | Everything dear again, all because of a few thieves.
b[role=merchant] #merch : They already have. I put mine up this morning. | A month? Two. | A few thieves and a lazy Watch.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : We'll go hungry, then. | Can't afford it anyway. | Thieves rob all of us.
b : I fear you're right. | Two, more like. | Aye.
a@merch : Of course you did. | Two. Gods. | Don't let them hear you.
a@poor : Not if I can help it. | Nor can I. | All of us.
a : I'm always right. | Two, then. Gods. | A few, and look.

scene w7c_cv_raid_fear
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a : I've a cousin who drives that road. | Do you think they'll come here? | I'll not travel this season.
b[warmth=warm] #warm : Is your cousin all right? Have you heard? | No. Not with the Watch at the gate. | Stay home. Safe.
b[temper=short] #short : Then your cousin should've stayed home. | Let them try. | Coward.
b : I hope they're all right. | Never. | Nor me.
a@warm : Not yet. I'm waiting. | I hope you're right. | I will.
a@short : That's cruel. | Brave words. | Call it what you like.
a : So do I. | I hope. | Then it's settled.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- More everyday work, for anyone

scene w7c_early_bird
when topic=work
a : I was here before the cock. | First in, every day. Nobody notices. | Who opened up? I thought I'd be first.
b[humour=dry] #dry : The cock's lazy. | I notice. I don't care, but I notice. | A ghost. A very punctual ghost.
b[drive=ambitious] #amb : Second. I'll beat you tomorrow. | Somebody does. Somebody important. | Me. I'm always first.
b : Well done. | I notice. | Me, I think.
a@dry : Lazier than you. | That'll do. | Very funny.
a@amb : Try it. | Who? | Not today.
a : Thank you. | Do you? | You!

scene w7c_counting
when topic=work
a : Seven, eight... Don't talk, I'm counting. | You made me lose count. | Count it for me, would you? My head's soup.
b[humour=merry] : Twelve, nine, forty... | You're welcome. | Nine. It's always nine.
b[honesty=sly] #sly : Shall I count for you? I'm very honest. | Sorry. It was nine. | I'll count. For a small fee.
b : Sorry. | Start again. | Give it here.
a@sly : Hush. | Was it? | I'll do it myself.
a : Hush. | From one, then. | Thank you.

scene w7c_heavy
when topic=work
a : This weighs more than I do. | Who packed this? A bear? | My back's gone. Somewhere. I'll find it later.
b[stage=old] : Lift with your legs. I learnt too late. | A careless bear. | Mine went years ago.
b[warmth=warm] #warm : Here, together. Lift. | Not me, I promise. Let me help. | Sit. I'll do it.
b : Everything is. | Some fool. | Go easy.
a@warm : Bless you. | Thanks. | No, no. I'll manage.
a : Now you tell me. | A fool with a grudge. | I'll try.

scene w7c_sharpen
when topic=work
a : Can I use your whetstone? | My blade's dull as a sermon. | Who's had my good knife? It's chipped.
b[honesty=sly] #sly : For a penny. | Dull? Ask the priest. | Not me. Probably.
b[temper=short] #short : Use your own. | Sharpen it, then. | Look elsewhere.
b : Go on. | Mine too. | Not me.
a@sly : A penny? You thief. | Ha. | Probably.
a@short : I would, if I had one. | With what? | Charming.
a : Thanks. I'll bring it back. | Bad as a sermon? | Someone has.

scene w7c_closing
when topic=work here.time=dusk|night a.working=yes
a : Shall we shut up shop? | That's enough for one day. | Put the shutters up. I'm done.
b[drive=ambitious] #amb : One more hour. | Never enough. | Not yet.
b[tired=yes] : Please. Yes. Please. | More than enough. | Gladly.
b : Aye. | Aye, it is. | Right.
a@amb : One hour. Not a breath more. | Enough for me. | Yes. Now.
a : Shutters, then. | Home. | Good.

scene w7c_opening
when topic=work here.time=dawn
a : Shutters up. Another day. | Sweep the step and we're open. | Light the fire, will you? My paws are frozen.
b[tired=yes] #tired : Already? I only just shut them. | My broom's asleep. | I'm frozen too.
b : Another day, another penny. | Swept. | Lit.
a@tired : Feels it. | Wake it up, then. | Then light it faster.
a : Here we go. | Open. | Bless you.

scene w7c_coin
when topic=work
a : Is this coin real? Bite it. | Somebody paid me with a clipped penny. | Look at this. Never seen a coin like it.
b[job=official|merchant] #merch : Clipped. Don't take it again. | It's light. Weigh it. | Foreign. Worth half.
b[stage=young] #pup : Can I keep it? | Can I bite it? | Shiny!
b : Looks real enough. | Clipped? Who? | Foreign, I'd say.
a@merch : I won't. | Light. I knew it. | Half. Typical.
a@pup : No. | No! | Very.
a : I'll bite it. | I wish I knew. | Worth something?

scene w7c_rain_day
when topic=work here.weather=rain|storm
a : Nobody's out in this. Dead day. | Rain's kept every customer indoors. | Stand by the fire. Nobody's coming.
b[role=merchant] : Dead. Deader than dead. | Not a soul. | Not one.
b[job=farmer|herder|woodcutter|laborer] : Dead? I'm soaked to the bone, out there. | Lucky them. | Lucky you, indoors.
b : Nice and quiet, then. | Let it rain. | Good.
a : Too quiet. | They're wise. | Warm.

scene w7c_fog_day
when topic=work here.weather=fog
a : Can't see the end of my own nose. | Fog's so thick I walked into the wall. | Lost the street in this.
b[humour=merry] #merry : Your nose is long. Good. | The wall started it. | Follow your nose.
b : Mind yourself. | Ouch. | Wait for it to lift.
a@merry : Very funny. | It did. | It's how I got lost.
a : I am. | It hurt. | I'll wait.

scene w7c_hot_day
when topic=work here.weather=clear here.season=summer
a : Too hot to think. | My fur's a blanket in this. | Is there any water left?
b[job=smith|baker|cook] #fire : Too hot? Come and stand at my fire. | Shed it. | Drink mine.
b : Sit in the shade. | Shear it off. | A little.
a@fire : No, thank you. | Ha. | Bless you.
a : There's no shade. | Ha. | Thanks.

scene w7c_snow_day
when topic=work here.weather=snow
a : Snowed in the path again. | My paws are blocks of ice. | Nobody's buying in this.
b[job=woodcutter] #wood : Shovel it with a smile. Snow sells my logs. | Wrap them. And buy some wood. | They'll buy wood. They're buying mine.
b : Shovel it. | Warm them by the fire. | Cold keeps them home.
a@wood : Easy for you. | From you, I suppose. | Lucky you.
a : I did. Twice. | I've nothing to warm them by. | It does. Every one of them.

scene w7c_crowd_busy
when topic=work here.crowd=crowd
a : Who are all these folk? | Can't move in here. | Somebody tell them to queue.
b[role=merchant] : Customers! Bless every one. | Good. Busy is good. | Queue? They'll walk.
b[temper=short] : Too many. Out! | Move, then. | Queue!
b : Busy day. | Squeeze through. | They never queue.
a : A whole town's worth. | I'll try. | Never.

scene w7c_crowd_quiet
when topic=work here.crowd=quiet
a : Quiet today. | Not a soul. | You could hear a pin drop.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Too quiet. | Not a sale, either. | Drop a coin. I'd hear that.
b : Nice, for once. | Rest, then. | Peaceful.
a@merch : It'll pick up. | Not one? | Ha.
a : For once. | Gladly. | Very.

scene w7c_good_tool
when topic=work
a : Look at this. New. Finest I've ever owned. | Bought myself a proper set at last. | Feel the balance on that.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Must have cost a fortune. | Lucky you. | Lovely. I'll never own one.
b[stage=old] : Look after it and it'll see you out. | Proper tools, proper work. | Balanced. Nice.
b : Lovely. | About time. | Nice weight.
a@poor : It did. Every penny. | Saved a year for it. | Never say never.
a : Isn't it. | Saved for it a year. | Isn't it just.

scene w7c_burnt
when topic=work
a : Burnt my paw on it. | Ow. Ow ow ow. | Don't touch that. Hot.
b[job=healer] : Cold water. Now. Don't argue. | Let me see. | Thanks for the warning.
b[humour=merry] #merry : That'll teach you. | Kiss it better? | Too late!
b : Cold water. | Ouch. | Thanks.
a@merry : It's throbbing! | Don't you dare. | Told you!
a : It's throbbing. | *shakes the paw* | Mind you don't.

scene w7c_tidy
when topic=work
a : Who left this mess? | You could tidy, you know. | Somebody's been at my bench.
b[honesty=frank] #frank : Me. Sorry. | I could. I won't. | I borrowed your bench. Sorry.
b[honesty=sly] : Rats. | Could I? | Rats again.
b : Not me. | I'll tidy later. | Wasn't me. Ask about.
a@frank : Well, tidy it. | Charming. | Ask next time.
a : Rats with paws. | Now. | Somebody did.

scene w7c_stranger_ask_work
when topic=work|smalltalk pair.band=strangers a.wealth=poor|destitute
a : Any work going? I'll do anything. | Does your master need a pair of paws? | I'm new in town. Know anyone hiring?
b[warmth=warm] : Ask at the yard. Tell them I sent you. | I'll ask. Come back tomorrow. | Try the carters. They always need backs.
b[warmth=cold] #cold : No. | Ask them yourself. | Not that I'd tell you.
b : Try the market. | Not that I know. | Ask at the inn.
a@cold : Right. | I will, then. | Thanks anyway.
a : Thank you. | I'll try. | Thank you kindly.

scene w7c_lunch
when topic=work here.time=day
a : What's in your pail today? | Swap you half? | I've brought too much bread.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Nothing much. | Gladly. | I'll take any.
b[wealth=rich] #rich : Cold pie. Have some. | Swap? Have it. | Bread? I've cheese.
b : Bread and onion. | Half's fair. | Share it.
a@rich : Don't mind if I do. | You're too kind. | Bread and cheese, then.
a : Same. | Half. | Here.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Still more of the everyday, for anyone at work

scene w7c_boots
when topic=work
a : My boots have gone through at the toe. | Look at this coat. More patch than coat. | I've worn a hole in my apron the shape of my belly.
b[wealth=rich] : Buy new, for pity's sake. | Get a proper one made. I'll tell you who. | Well, it's a handsome belly.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Stuff them with straw. Mine are. | Patches are honest. | Turn it round. Wear the back.
b[job=crafter] #craft : Bring them by. I'll do it at cost. | I can fix that. Restday. | Leave it with me.
b : Get them mended. | Patch the patches. | Ha! So you have.
a@craft : You're a gem. | Restday, then. | Bless you.
a : Next month. | I will. | Laugh, go on.

scene w7c_mouser
when topic=work
a : The cat caught three rats in the store last night. | Somebody's been feeding the yard cat. It's useless now. | There's a dog sleeping on the sacks again.
b[warmth=warm] : Good cat. Give it a bit of something. | Me. Sorry. It looked so thin. | Let it sleep. It's cold out.
b[temper=short] : Good. Now catch the rest. | Stop it, whoever it is. | Kick it off.
b : Earns its keep, that one. | Fat cats don't hunt. | Shoo it off.
a : Better than some of us. | Well, it's fat now. | It looks so comfortable, though.

scene w7c_wasp
when topic=work here.season=summer|autumn
a : There's a wasp in here. Where'd it go? | Something stung me! | Don't move. It's on your ear.
b[temper=nervy] : Where? Where? Get it out! | Ow! Me too! | Get it off. Get it off!
b[humour=merry] : It's behind you. No, the other behind. | Rub dock leaf on it and cry. | It likes you.
b : Open the door. | Show me. | ...Has it gone?
a : It's gone. I think. | Swelling already. Look. | Gone.

scene w7c_read_order
when topic=work
a : Can you read this? Somebody's left an order. | What does this word say? | My letters are poor. Read me this.
b[job=scholar|official|priest] #read : Of course. "Twelve, by Restday, and no excuses." | That says "urgent". It's underlined. | Give it here. Hm. Rude, but clear.
b[talk=quiet] #quiet : ...Sorry. I can't. | I don't know. | No.
b : Twelve of something, by Restday. | "Urgent", I think. | Something about pay.
a@read : Twelve! By Restday! | Lovely. | Rude how?
a@quiet : Never mind. | I'll ask someone else. | Fine.
a : Twelve! | Lovely. | Pay? Good.

scene w7c_measure
when topic=work
a : It's too short. I measured it twice! | Who cut this? It's crooked as a dog's leg. | It doesn't fit. Nothing fits today.
b[temper=short] : Then measure three times. | Not me. | Make it fit.
b[humour=dry] : Twice wrong, then. | A crooked dog, by the look. | Nothing ever fits. That's the trade.
b : Start again. | Ask who had the saw. | Shave a bit off.
a : I'll start again. | Nobody owns up. | Fine.

scene w7c_late_delivery
when topic=work
a : The delivery's late again. | Where's that cart? It said dawn. | I've nothing to work with till it comes.
b[job=carter] : Don't look at me. Mine's on time. Mostly. | The road's half mud. | Sit tight. They're coming.
b[temper=short] : Then shout at the carter. | Dawn where? | Find something.
b : It'll come. | Bad roads. | Sweep, then.
a : I've shouted. It didn't come. | Always. | Doing nothing. Lovely.

scene w7c_payday_plans
when topic=work a.shift=during|after b.business=none b.stage=adult|old
a : What'll you do with your #wages#? | Paid tomorrow. I've spent it already, in my head. | One more day to pay.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Rent. Then nothing. | So have I. On rent. | It'll be gone by the next day.
b[humour=merry] : Ale. Then more ale. Then soup. | On what? Tell me. | One more day of being poor.
b[drive=ambitious] : Save it. Every penny. | I'm putting it by for a stall. | Spend it on a better tool.
b : Pay what I owe. | Same. | Hold on.
a : Sensible. | A new hat. And pie. | Tomorrow, then.

scene w7c_saving
when topic=work a.stage=adolescent|adult
a : I'm saving for a good coat. | Six more months and I'll have enough for a stall. | I'm putting by a penny a day. For the wedding.
b[warmth=warm] : Good for you! I'll help you choose. | You'll get there. | A wedding! Whose?
b[honesty=sly] #sly : Keep it under the floor. Not in the house. | A stall? Mine's for sale. | A penny a day? Lend me one.
b : Good. | Six months goes quick. | Whose wedding?
a@sly : Under the floor. Right. | Yours? No thank you. | Not likely.
a : Thank you. | I hope. | Mine. Maybe.

scene w7c_own_shop
when topic=work a.drive=ambitious|restless
a : One day, my own name over a door. | I'll not work for another wolf forever. | When I'm my own master, I'll do it properly.
b[drive=content] : Why? It's a bother. Let others worry. | I like working for someone. Less to fret over. | Properly's hard.
b[stage=old] : I said that. Forty years ago. | Save first. Then dream. | We'll see.
b : Good. | Go on, then. | Will you?
a : You'll see. | Watch me. | I will.

scene w7c_shop_closing
when topic=work
a : Did you hear the chandler's shutting? | They say the old bakery's closing for good. | Another shop boarded on our street.
b[business=failing] #fail : That'll be me soon. | Don't. I'm next. | Next week, mine.
b[role=merchant] #merch : Their customers'll come to me. | Good. Less competition. Sorry. | Shame. Good spot, too.
b : Shame. | Twenty years they had it. | Hard times.
a@fail : Don't say that. | It won't come to that. | Hold on. Something'll turn.
a@merch : Vulture. | Sorry? You're not. | It was, too.
a : End of something. | And now look. | Harder every month.

scene w7c_weights
when topic=work
a : The official's coming round to check the weights. | They're testing scales today. Is yours honest? | Somebody was fined for short weight.
b[honesty=sly] #sly : Mine's honest. Very honest. Let me just adjust it. | As honest as anyone's. | Unlucky.
b[honesty=frank] : Let them. I've nothing to hide. | Always. | Good. Serves them right.
b : Let them. | Course. | Who?
a@sly : Adjust it how? | That's not saying much. | Unlucky? They were caught.
a : Good. | Hm. We'll see. | The one on the corner.

scene w7c_pickpocket
when topic=work here.place=market|street
a : Watch your purse. There's a light paw about. | Saw a pup lift a purse just now. Quick as a fish. | Somebody's been at my takings.
b[role=guard] #guard : Point them out. | Which way did they go? | I'll watch your stall.
b[honesty=sly] : I saw nothing. | Clever pup. | Not me.
b : Thanks for the warning. | Where? | Lock it away.
a@guard : Gone now. Into the crowd. | That way. Quick. | Thank you.
a : Keep it close. | Gone. | I will.

scene w7c_lend_coin
when topic=work pair.band=acquaintances|friends
a : Lend me a penny till Restday? | Could you spare a few coppers? | I'm short. Just this week.
b[wealth=rich] #give : Here. Don't worry about it. | A few? Here's more. | Take it.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #none : I've less than you. | Spare? Ha. | Me too.
b[honesty=guarded] #why : What for? | How many's a few? | Again?
b : Restday. Promise? | Here. | Just this week.
a@give : You're a good sort. | Bless you. | I'll pay it back.
a@none : Never mind. | Sorry I asked. | Then we're both short.
a@why : Bread. | Three. Four. | Last time. Truly.
a : Promise. | Bless you. | I swear it.

scene w7c_old_tool
when topic=work
a : This hammer was #grandad#'s. | Old tool, this. Older than me. | The handle's been changed five times. The head never.
b[stage=old] #old : They made them proper then. | Like me. | Same as my axe.
b : Still works. | Look after it. | Then is it the same hammer?
a@old : They don't make them like that now. | Ha. Like you. | Same story, then.
a : Better than new. | It'll see me out. | ...Don't.

scene w7c_pups_underfoot
when topic=work a.parent=yes
a : The pups were underfoot all morning. | Mine wants to help. Helping is worse. | Brought the little one. Couldn't leave them.
b[stage=young] #pup : I'm not underfoot! I'm helping! | I can help! | Hello!
b[warmth=warm] : Let them. They learn by watching. | Give them a broom. | They're welcome.
b[temper=short] : Keep them clear of the fire. | Send them home. | Mind they don't touch anything.
b : They're quick, at that age. | It's sweet. | Fair enough.
a@pup : You're underfoot. | Help by sitting still. | Say hello properly.
a : I'm trying. | It's slow. | Good as gold. Mostly.

scene w7c_caught_napping
when topic=work
a : Were you asleep? | Wake up! | You're snoring on the job.
b[tired=yes] : I was resting my eyes. Hard. | I'm awake. I'm awake. | Only a little.
b[humour=merry] : Thinking. Deeply. | I was listening to the wood grow. | Snoring's a kind of singing.
b : No. | I'm up! | Was I?
a : Hm. | Good. | Loudly.

scene w7c_customer_gossip
when topic=work a.business=thriving|steady|failing
a : A customer told me the strangest thing today. | You hear everything behind a counter. | Old so-and-so came in. Talked an hour.
b[talk=chatty] : What? Tell me! | Tell me everything. | Talked! About what?
b[honesty=guarded] #guard : Best not repeat it. | Then keep it there. | Did they buy anything?
b : Oh? | I bet. | About what?
a@guard : Later, then. | I'll try. | A button.
a : I'll tell you later. | It's true. | Their knees. For an hour.

scene w7c_steward
when topic=work a.house
a : The House steward came round with the ledger. | Steward's counted every nail in the yard. | They want the accounts by Restday.
b[self.house] : Ours too. Counted twice. | Always counting, that one. | Again?
b : Find anything? | Every nail? | Restday!
a : Nothing. This time. | Every one. | Restday. I'll be up all night.

scene w7c_other_towns
when topic=work here.region=frosthollow|coldwater|oakhaven|mirebridge
a : In Larkfield, they say, a stall pays twice what it does here. | Ridgemere work pays better, I'm told. | Southmeadow folk work half as hard. All that sun.
b[from=larkfield] : True. And the rent's three times. | So I'm told. | Southmeadow? They work. Slowly, but they work.
b[from=southmeadow] : Larkfield charges twice for everything, too. | Ridgemere pays. Ridgemere charges. | Half as hard? Come and pick apples and say that.
b[from=frosthollow] : Try a day in the mines. Then tell me who works. | Pays more, costs more. | Sun's lovely. Try snow.
b[from=ridgemere] : And costs double. | It does. Ask anyone. | Half as hard. Twice as happy.
b : They say a lot. | Is it? | I've heard.
a : Tempting, though. | So they say. | Sounds nice.

scene w7c_lamp_oil
when topic=work here.time=dusk|night
a : Lamp oil's half gone already. | Can't see a thing. More light! | My eyes are going in this light.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Work in the dark. I do. | Light costs. | Mine are half gone already.
b : Fill it, then. | Here. | Rest them.
a@poor : In the dark? Not likely. | Everything costs. | Then we're a pair.
a : With what? | Thanks. | I'll try.

scene w7c_big_job_done
when topic=work
a : Done! The big one's done! | Finished it. Three weeks I've been at it. | It's done. Come and look.
b[warmth=warm] : Oh, it's beautiful! Well done! | Three weeks! You must be proud. | Show me!
b[warmth=cold] #cold : About time. | Took you long enough. | I'll look later.
b[humour=merry] : Let's drink to it! | Three weeks? I'd have done it in two. | Ooh!
b : Well done. | At last. | Let's see.
a@cold : Charming. | Three weeks of good work. | Suit yourself.
a : Thank you. | Three weeks, and worth it. | There.

scene w7c_charm
when topic=work
a : Where's my lucky stone? I always work with it on the bench. | I touched wood this morning and still dropped everything. | My lucky nail's gone missing.
b[piety=devout] #dev : Pray. Stones don't listen. | The Bright One doesn't need wood. | Trust the Bright One, not nails.
b[humour=dry] : It's lucky somewhere else now. | Should've touched more wood. | A nail can't be lucky. It's a nail.
b : Under the bench? | Bad luck. | It'll turn up.
a@dev : Stones can't hurt. | Wood can't hurt either. | Both, to be safe.
a : Not there. | Very bad. | Hope so.

scene w7c_teach_me
when topic=work pair.band=acquaintances|friends|strangers
a : Could you teach me your trade? | How long did it take you to learn that? | Would you take an apprentice?
b[master=yes] : I've one already. One's plenty. | Years. Still learning. | I've one. Ask me in a year.
b[warmth=warm] : I could show you a little. Come by. | Years. But you'd be quicker. | Maybe. Come and watch.
b[warmth=cold] : No. | Too long for you. | No.
b : It's not easy. | Years. | Perhaps.
a : I'm a quick learner. | Years! | I'll ask again.

scene w7c_mud
when topic=work here.weather=rain|storm|snow
a : Who tracked mud all through? | Wipe your paws! | The floor's a pig-sty.
b[humour=merry] : Mud's free. Enjoy it. | They don't wipe. Nobody wipes. | Oink.
b : Customers. | Sorry. | I'll sweep.
a : Every last one of them. | Wipe them. | Please.

scene w7c_quiet_moment
when topic=work
a : Listen. Nothing. Lovely. | This is the best part of the day. The quiet part. | I like it when it's just us.
b[talk=chatty] #chat : Isn't it? Now, did I tell you... | It is. Let me tell you why. | Me too! Now then...
b : Lovely. | It is. | Me too.
a@chat : ...It was. | ...It was, a moment ago. | ...Never mind.
a : Shh. Listen. | *settles back* | Mm.

scene w7c_wrong_order
when topic=work
a : They ordered blue. I made blue. Now they want green. | Customer changed their mind. Again. | They wanted it smaller. After I'd finished.
b[temper=short] : Charge them double. | Throw it at them. | Tell them no.
b[humour=dry] : Make it blue-green. Everyone loses. | Minds are like the weather. | Cut it in half. Two small ones.
b : Customers. | Typical. | Charge for it.
a : Next time, I'll ask twice. | Every time. | I will.

scene w7c_good_customer
when topic=work
a : A customer paid me extra. Just because. | Somebody said my work was the best in town. | Old dear brought me a pie for mending her chair.
b[warmth=warm] : Oh, that's lovely. You deserve it. | You are, you know. | Bless her.
b[honesty=sly] : Did they? I'll send them more of mine. | Who? I'll pay them to say it of me. | Share the pie?
b : That's rare. | Nice. | That's kind.
a : It made my week. | It was. | Still warm, too.

scene w7c_thief_tools
when topic=work
a : Somebody stole my best saw. | Lost a whole morning looking for my mallet. | Tools keep walking off.
b[role=guard] : Report it. We'll look. | Lost, or taken? | I'll ask about.
b[honesty=sly] : Stole? Or lent and forgot? | Look in the river. | Tools have legs. Funny, that.
b : Lock them up. | Found it? | Thieves.
a : I'll lock the rest up, anyway. | I'd like to know. | Somebody's got a nice set by now.

scene w7c_sore_back
when topic=work a.stage=adult|old
a : My back's not right. | Bent over all day. I'll be crooked as a crook. | I creak when I stand.
b[job=healer] #heal : Warm stones on it tonight. | Lie flat. Not soft. Flat. | Come and see me.
b[stage=old] : Wait till it's every day. | Mine's been crooked for years. | Me too.
b : Stretch it. | Stand up straight now and then. | Rest it.
a@heal : Warm stones. Right. | Flat. Right. | I will.
a : I'll try. | Easy said. | If only.
